  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>S</mi></math> be the set of all real numbers. Then, the relation <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></math> on <math><mi>S</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "reflexive and symmetric but not transitive",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "reflexive and transitive but not symmetric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "reflexive, transitive and symmetric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of the above",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></math><br />(i)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>(ii)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>(iii)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math><br />It is clear that the given relation on <math><mi>S</mi></math> is reflexive, symmetric but not transitive.</p>"
